      "extract": "[]{#sub.motivation label=\"sub.motivation\"} Ideal triangulations of 3-manifolds with torus boundary components were introduced by Thurston [@Thurston] as a convenient way to describe and effectively compute [@snappy] complete hyperbolic structures on 3-manifolds. To do so, one assigns a complex number different from 0 or 1 to each tetrahedron and a polynomial equation around each edge of the triangulation. These",
